P3692R4 [SOLVED]
Description: The entire abstract is missing. Why is it missing?
Root cause: PDF paper. TOC body protection in pipeline.py counted only
first-line words (nxt_fl.split()) instead of full paragraph words
(nxt_sec.text.split()). P3692R4's abstract paragraph has 170 words total
but only 8 on the first line, failing the _TOC_BODY_PROTECT_MIN_WORDS=10
threshold. The abstract body was correctly extracted by MuPDF but then
stripped as a TOC artifact.
Fix: Changed nxt_fl.split() to nxt_sec.text.split() in pipeline.py.
Simulated across all 124 PDFs: only P3692R4 changes (abstract body now
present), 122 others identical, 0 regressions.
File: packages/tomd/src/tomd/lib/pdf/pipeline.py.
P4043R0 [SOLVED]
Description: The abstract is empty. The "Abstract" heading is extracted,
but the text that follows it is not.
Root cause: HTML paper. Abstract body was correctly extracted. The actual
issue was a metadata leak: bold-formatted metadata lines
(**Document number**: P4043R0, **Date**: ..., **Authors**: ...,
**Audience**: ...) appeared in the Markdown body because
_REDUNDANT_META_RE and _FREEFORM_META_LABEL_RE in shared.py did not
match Markdown bold markers (**...**).
Fix: Extended both regexes with \*{0,2} anchors to match optional bold
markers. Also added "Document number" as a label in _FREEFORM_META_LABEL_RE.
Verified across 270 markdowns: 6 legitimate metadata leaks now stripped,
zero false positives. File: packages/tomd/src/tomd/lib/shared.py.
P4151R1 [SOLVED]
Description: The abstract is missing. It was present before; a recent
code change led to this error.
Root cause: PDF paper. Abstract body is genuinely short (5 words:
"std::execution::affine_on should be named std::execution::affine.").
total_words=5 < _TOC_BODY_PROTECT_MIN_WORDS=10. The word-count threshold
rejected the body as a TOC artifact.
Fix: Abstract-specific threshold bypass. When the protected heading is
"abstract" (case-insensitive), the _TOC_BODY_PROTECT_MIN_WORDS check is
skipped for the first body paragraph. All other KNOWN_SECTIONS retain the
threshold of 10 to guard against TOC artifacts. Simulated across all 124
PDFs: only P4151R0 and P4151R1 change (abstract body recovered, 5 words
each), 122 others identical, 0 regressions.
Also affects P4151R0 (older revision, same abstract, also fixed).
File: packages/tomd/src/tomd/lib/pdf/pipeline.py.

P4042R0 [SOLVED]
Description: Abstract body missing. Root cause: _detect_body_size in
structure.py miscalculates body font size (9.0pt from LMRoman9-Regular
wording text instead of 10.7pt Lato-Light prose). This causes the
actual abstract body (10.7pt) to be classified as HEADING with
Confidence.LOW, and the TOC protection loop breaks on HEADING.
Fix: In pipeline.py TOC protection loop, when the protected heading
is "abstract" and the first following section is a LOW-confidence
HEADING, reclassify it as PARAGRAPH (kind=PARAGRAPH, heading_level=0)
and protect it. Simulated across all 124 PDFs: only P4042R0 changes
(abstract body recovered, 11 words), 123 others identical, 0
regressions. File: packages/tomd/src/tomd/lib/pdf/pipeline.py.
Extraction Boundary Issues / Over-Extraction
Issues where the abstract extracts correctly at first, but doesn't stop where it
should, pulling in metadata, unrelated paragraphs, or swallowing other sections.

P3977R0 [SOLVED]
Description: PDF paper. Title and metadata (Document, Date, Audience,
Reply to) appeared as plaintext in the body.
Root cause: _FREEFORM_META_LABEL_RE in shared.py did not match bare
"Document:" (only "Document number"/"Document No."). Additionally,
continuation detection required indentation or comma prefix, but PDF
metadata often has the value on the next line without indentation
(e.g. "Date:\nJanuary 22, 2026").
Fix: (1) Changed regex to make "number"/"No." optional after
"Document" so bare "Document:" matches. (2) Extended continuation
logic: when a metadata label line ends with ":" (value on next line),
the next non-blank non-structural non-label line is treated as the
value and also removed. Simulated across 270 markdowns: only P3977R0
changes, 0 regressions.
Additionally fixed: (3) Plaintext title echo stripped by extending
strip_leading_h1 to match non-ATX titles (no # prefix) via fuzzy
_titles_match. (4) Bare "Abstract" promoted to ## Abstract when it
appears as the first content line after frontmatter (PDF structurer
missed the heading). Both changes in shared.py, verified with golden
tests (0 regressions).
File: packages/tomd/src/tomd/lib/shared.py.

